                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "More of the same enjoyable gameplay as the first Luxor game, except there's now a Scorpion powerup.\n\n[h1]WARNING![/h1]\nBecause MumboJumbo could not be bothered to patch the following two bugs out of the Steam version of this game:\n\n[list]\n[*]Stage 9 in Adventure mode ends prematurely (One of the levels is misread as another from the previous Luxor HD game)\n[*]The path in the Anubis Aegyptus map is not optimised for widescreen (You can directly see how the spheres come in)\n[/list]\n\nI strongly suggest downloading QuickBMS and the MumboJumbo.bms script, and then extracting the data.mjz file before patching the bugs out.\n\nAfter extraction, you should find where the two bugs are located:\n\n[olist]\n[*]For Stage 9 to play properly, jump into the directory:\nLuxor Amun Rising HD\\data\\levels\\adventure_luxor_ar\nThere, you will find \"level_9_4.lvl\". Make an edit through Notepad or whatever. replace \"imhotepsfolly\" with \"crossingthereedsea\" and voila! The stage should now play properly!\n[*]To optimise the entrance in the Anubis Aegyptus map for widescreen displays, jump into the directory:\nLuxor Amun Rising HD\\data\\maps\\anubisaegyptus\nThere, you should edit the path.obj file with Notepad in the following manner: Replace \"v 820 -40 0\" to \"v 1020 -40 0\" \n[/olist]",
